  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, radius $=r$, arc length $=\\ell$\n$2 \\mathrm{r}+\\ell=20 \\Rightarrow \\ell=20-2 \\mathrm{r}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{A}=\\frac{1}{2}\\mathrm{r}^{2} \\theta = \\frac{1}{2} \\ell \\mathrm{r} \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dA}}{\\mathrm{dr}}=\\frac{1}{2}(20-4 \\mathrm{r})=0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{r}=5 \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{r}=5 \\mathrm{~m}\\right.$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/JRbJrKnFUlvZADQFyXNXNZKKvSVzhvIuDZAe_uq25ls.original.fullsize.png\">",
